    "description": "Add a quick-create entry for Operator to the Global Actions \"+\" menu (top nav), alongside the standard New Task / New Event / New Contact / New Opportunity / New Lead entries, so users can create a new Operator record without navigating to the Accounts list view first.\n\nCONTEXT\n\nOperator is a custom record type on Account, not a standalone object, so it doesn't appear in the Global Actions \"+\" menu by default the way New Contact or New Opportunity do. Users currently have to go through the Accounts list view (or an existing Operator record) to start a new one.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n\n1\\. A \"New Operator\" action is available from the Global Actions \"+\" menu.\n\n2\\. Selecting it opens record creation pre-set to the Operator record type (no manual record-type picker step).\n\n3\\. Action is visible to the same users/profiles who can currently create Operator records today (no permission expansion).\n\nRELATED\n\nCompanion asks from the same feedback pass, not in scope here:\n\nName field surfaced as a required input when creating a new Operator\n\nAbility to create the associated Contact inline during Operator creation, instead of a separate \"create new contact\" window\n\nSOURCE\n\nEmily Vandenberg, Wagertech feedback — Operator & Partner Record Pages doc, WAGERTECH Feedback OPERATOR section: \"in the '+' button menu top for the UI, add links to quickly create a new Operator\"\n\n[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rA6wTcVOFdstfhumSpffYWSMQ711nvkVZtUMUVA0YfI/edit](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rA6wTcVOFdstfhumSpffYWSMQ711nvkVZtUMUVA0YfI/edit)\n\nCreated 2026-09-03 from the Operator & Partner Record Pages feedback review.",
